From fcef95853390e682c2a3928791e83fc481ae2bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joaco2382 <104966815+Joaco2382@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:34:36 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: send uniforms with the type the linked program uses

The uniform parser doesn't evaluate #if blocks, so a name declared with one
type in an inactive branch of one stage and with another type in the other
stage was registered with the first type found. clouds.vert declares
"vec2 g_CloudSpeeds" under PERSPECTIVE == 0 and clouds.frag "vec4
g_CloudSpeeds" under the #else: with PERSPECTIVE = 1 the engine called
glUniform2fv on a vec4 every frame (GL_INVALID_OPERATION).

- After linking, the type of every active uniform is read with
  glGetActiveUniform. When both stages declare a name with different types,
  the declaration that matches the program is used (also for its default
  value), and values are always sent with the program's type.
- An OpenGL error left behind by earlier calls no longer makes --screenshot
  fail: pending errors are logged and cleared before reading the pixels.
  That stale error is why workshop 2228173242 captured as a black image.

Tests: UniformTypes (3 cases) with the clouds declarations.
